  "copula": "Copula drills are sentence translations, not closed forms. Used only as cloze of the leading copula particle (Irish Is/Ní/An/Ba/Níor/Níorbh, Welsh Nid/Ai, Scottish Gaelic An and 'S ann, Manx She) or the copula verb (Breton eo, Cornish yw) when the English translation fixes the polarity and tense. Affirmative Welsh ydw/ydy/yw drills are skipped (ydw/wyf and ydy/yw are all valid). Drills with English such as 'Is it true that:' or an sc-/sp- lenition error in the sentence are skipped.",
  "welsh_future_skipped": "Welsh future cells are pronoun-bearing colloquial forms (cana i) and the synthetic future has no listing, so the future is not asked; subjunctive covers five verbs and is skipped.",
